N-2a-3 (docs/NOCTURNE.md section 6.5) -- make SDL's dummy audio driver the
AUTO-SELECTED fallback on Thylacine.

Upstream keeps DUMMYAUDIO demand_only (SDL_TRUE): SDL_AudioInit's
auto-selection loop `continue`s past it, so with no other driver available
SDL_Init(SDL_INIT_AUDIO) fails with "No available audio device". On
Thylacine a soundless boot is an ordinary configuration (THYLACINE_NO_AUDIO,
a machine without the virtio-sound function): the thylacine driver's Init
declines when /srv/nocturne is absent, and every SDL program that inits
audio as part of a combined SDL_Init -- DOSBox-X's E_Exit on failure being
the worked case its old 0004 patch papered over with setenv
SDL_AUDIODRIVER=dummy -- would die. With demand_only false under
__thylacine__ the dummy driver, last in bootstrap[], is reached exactly when
thylacine declined, so such a program runs silently instead. An explicit
SDL_AUDIODRIVER still wins (the named-driver path is unchanged).

One hunk against the pristine vendored tree.

--- a/src/audio/dummy/SDL_dummyaudio.c
+++ b/src/audio/dummy/SDL_dummyaudio.c
@@ -54,7 +54,13 @@
 }
 
 AudioBootStrap DUMMYAUDIO_bootstrap = {
-    "dummy", "SDL dummy audio driver", DUMMYAUDIO_Init, SDL_TRUE
+    "dummy", "SDL dummy audio driver", DUMMYAUDIO_Init,
+#if defined(__thylacine__)
+    /* auto-selected when the thylacine driver declined (no /srv/nocturne) */
+    SDL_FALSE
+#else
+    SDL_TRUE
+#endif
 };
 
 #endif
